NekoSU
======

NekoSU is a custom Android root manager and kernel module for Samsung devices.
It combines a Baka-SU style manager UI with a Samsung-aware KernelSU kernel
engine (KDP / RKP / DEFEX bypass, late-load).

This product includes software developed by the following projects.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. KernelSU
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Source:  https://github.com/tiann/KernelSU
License: GNU General Public License v3.0

The kernel module (`kernel/`), the userspace daemon (`userspace/ksud`,
`userspace/ksuinit`), the UAPI headers (`uapi/`) and the low-level parts of
the manager (`manager/app/src/main/cpp/`) are derived from KernelSU.

Copyright (C) KernelSU contributors.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. KernelSU Samsung fork (diabl0w)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Source:  https://github.com/diabl0w/KernelSU
License: GNU General Public License v3.0

Samsung compatibility layer used by NekoSU:
  - `kernel/compat/kdp.c`      — Knox Defender Platform bypass
  - `kernel/compat/rkp.c`      — Real-time Kernel Protection bypass
  - `kernel/compat/defex.c`    — DEFEX bypass
  - `kernel/compat/jailbreak.c`, `kernel/compat/jailbreak.h`
  - Samsung-specific changes in `kernel/core/init.c`,
    `kernel/feature/selinux_hide.c`, `kernel/hook/**`,
    `kernel/feature/sucompat.c`
  - userspace `late-load --soft-reboot` support

Copyright (C) diabl0w and contributors.

